WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.713
Care Gap Explorer uses recorded A1C results

00:00:02.753 --> 00:00:06.980
to identify patients who may be missing current monitoring.

00:00:07.603 --> 00:00:12.591
The application looks back 365 days from a fixed data date.

00:00:12.848 --> 00:00:18.090
A patient with an A1C result inside that window is classified as current.

00:00:18.431 --> 00:00:23.743
If a patient has an earlier A1C result, but none within the 365-day window,

00:00:23.783 --> 00:00:27.801
the application classifies the patient as overdue.

00:00:28.299 --> 00:00:31.949
If no A1C result appears anywhere in the available data,

00:00:31.989 --> 00:00:35.206
the patient is classified as never tested.

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:39.895
In this synthetic cohort, 91 patients are current

00:00:39.935 --> 00:00:46.627
and 25 have an open monitoring gap: 4 overdue and 21 with no recorded A1C.

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:51.946
These statuses describe monitoring under the application's measure definition.

00:00:52.323 --> 00:00:57.350
They are not diagnoses and do not determine what treatment a patient should receive.
